---
import SiteLayout from "../../layouts/SiteLayout.astro";
import pages from "../../data/pages.json";
---

<SiteLayout metadata={pages["/security/"]}>
  <main id="main">
    <div class="wrap">
      <nav class="breadcrumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
        <a href="/">Home</a> <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>{" "}
        <span aria-current="page">
          Otto Security, AI Review &amp; Data Questions
        </span>
      </nav>
      <section class="tool-hero">
        <div class="eyebrow">Trust & review</div>
        <h1>
          Clear decisions.
          <br />
          Careful handling of data.
        </h1>
        <p>
          Understand the review controls Otto describes, and get specific
          answers about the data your practice entrusts to a system.
        </p>
      </section>
      <section class="product-section">
        <h2>What Otto publicly describes.</h2>
        <div class="product-grid">
          <section class="panel">
            <h3>Clinician confirmation</h3>
            <p>
              The public workflow requires confirmation before proposed
              structured data writes to the longitudinal record.
            </p>
          </section>
          <section class="panel">
            <h3>Draft attribution</h3>
            <p>
              Otto describes an AI provenance badge and a note-review process
              where the clinician can edit and sign.
            </p>
          </section>
          <section class="panel">
            <h3>Correction and recovery</h3>
            <p>
              The site describes correction tracking and a fallback to
              re-recording or manual entry if a note fails.
            </p>
          </section>
        </div>
      </section>
      <section class="product-section">
        <h2>Questions to resolve before using patient data.</h2>
        <p>
          These items need written, Otto-specific answers. A general product
          description does not establish contractual protections or a complete
          security posture.
        </p>
        <div class="faq-list">
          <details open>
            <summary>Business associate agreement and service scope</summary>
            <p>
              Request the applicable BAA and confirm which Otto services, AI
              processing, telehealth, and support workflows it covers. BAA
              availability has not been verified in this review.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary>Recording consent, retention, and deletion</summary>
            <p>
              Confirm how consent is captured, how long audio and transcripts
              persist, how deletion works, and whether backups have a different
              retention period. Ask what happens when a patient declines
              recording.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary>AI providers and use of data</summary>
            <p>
              Request the subprocessor list and contractual limits on training
              use, human access, retention, and regional processing. Do not
              infer these terms from the presence of an AI feature.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary>Access controls and incident response</summary>
            <p>
              Confirm authentication, roles, audit logging, encryption, account
              offboarding, and incident notification procedures. Ask which
              controls your practice can configure.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary>Record export and account closure</summary>
            <p>
              Request an export demonstration and written terms for format,
              timing, retention, and deletion after cancellation or the end of a
              trial.
            </p>
          </details>
        </div>
        <a
          class="button outline"
          href="/security/review-checklist.txt"
          download
        >
          Download the review questions ↓
        </a>
        <div class="review-note">
          This page is a review draft. BAA, retention, encryption, subprocessor,
          and model-training claims must be confirmed by Otto’s security and
          legal owners before this becomes a public security statement.
        </div>
        <p class="micro">
          References:{" "}
          <a href="https://otto.tebra.com/">Otto’s public product page</a> ·{" "}
          <a href="https://www.tebra.com/platform-privacy-policy">
            Tebra platform privacy policy
          </a>{" "}
          ·{" "}
          <a href="https://www.tebra.com/tebra-terms-of-service">Tebra terms</a>
          . Confirm each document’s applicability to your Otto service.
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>
    <section class="cta-section">
      <div class="wrap">
        <div class="cta">
          <div>
            <h2>Make more room for the work you love.</h2>
            <p>
              See how Otto brings notes, scheduling, telehealth, and payments
              into your practice day.
            </p>
          </div>
          <a class="button light" href="/waitlist/">
            Join the waitlist <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
</SiteLayout>
